# set test time
# Year is pinned (not left at TIME's own wall-clock default) so the
# Moon's own rendered position/phase - Moon3D.draw() runs on every
# frame, unlike the Sun-shading path views.svs's own comment covers -
# can't drift from one baseline regeneration to the next just because
# of which real year happens to be current when this runs (see
# funcs.MoonPosition's own comment on SHADE_EPOCH_DAY). 2026 matches
# terrain.svs's own pinned year, for one consistent year across this
# whole test suite rather than picking a different one per script.
#
# Hour is pinned too, same reasoning: SHADE_HOUR_ANGLE's own
# bare-construction default is now the real wall-clock hour
# (shadeViewport3D.pde's own hour()-seeded default, not a fixed
# constant anymore), so without this it would drift from one baseline
# regeneration to the next depending on what time of day this happens
# to run - 10 matches SHADE_HOUR_ANGLE's own previous hardcoded
# default, so this keeps every existing committed baseline valid.
Year 2026
Month 1
Day 15
Hour 10

# clear default model
Delete all

3d-model 3

Delete All Model2Ds

Tree1 m=0 x=-20 y=-10 z=0 h=10 degree=8 seed=0 r=0 tilt=60 twist=137.5 ratio=0.8 base=2 trunk=1 leaf=0.2
Tree2 m=1 x=0 y=-20 z=0 h=15

Person m=5 x=-20 y=-20 z=0
Person m=6 x=-15 y=-20 z=0
Person m=7 x=-20 y=-15 z=0

Select nothing

Hide Sun Path

